{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/138976-what-source-of-energy-power-is-the-strongest","id":138976,"title":"What source of energy/power is the strongest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T22:47:59-07:00","id":138976,"title":"What source of energy/power is the strongest?","content":"a friend of mine invented a technique in which a Garou erased a point of Gnosis causing agravated damage (spirutual damage) to his sorroundings...and then the discussion started...What sort of supernatural energy is the most powerful in all of WoD ?<br /> <br /> I always thought that both Blood and Phatos were the weakest while the strongest would be Faith (D:tF) but what you guys think, how would be the scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:25:05-07:00","id":139083,"title":"","content":"Quintessence or Chi are the strongest, as in their respective gamelines, these are fundamental, universal forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:31:29-07:00","id":139089,"title":"","content":"It very much depends on how you want to define &quot;strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, in terms of innate abilities, Rage probably wins. It has some crappy drawbacks, but it is easy to regain.<br /> <br /> Vitae is probably a close runner up but it depends how well you can apply the blood bond. Physical buffing and healing are nice, but can drain out pretty fast.<br /> <br /> Beyond that... it very much depends on the powers the character has doesn't it? A vampire with very few vitae using Disciplines doesn't find it that useful. A werewolves Gift selection (or reliance on Talens/Fetishes/Rites) with very much dictate how potent Rage or Gnosis will be in their hands.<br /> <br /> Quintessence, by itself, does squat. Combine it with Spheres and lowering the difficulties of magic? Pretty damned potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:00:24-07:00","id":139234,"title":"","content":"Quintessence is the most powerful. Not only can it be converted into and out of other supernatural forms (vitae, gnosis, power, etc.), but it is the actual building block of the entire Tellurian.<br /> <br /> It is universal and unavoidable. All things living or not have Quintessence, which can not be said of any other energy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you mean in a munchkin kind of way, I would say vitae. The blood-bond is far too amazing and EASY to be ignored. Keep in mind though... the same thing can be achieved with Quintessence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T09:20:53-07:00","id":141634,"title":"","content":"as far as i'm aware, most of the power sources in oWoD are pretty much the same thing viewed through cultural lenses. in the werewolf storyteller handbook, while describing mages the fury telling the story says they are draining it for it's gnosis. while according to changelings mages and werewolves guard sources of natural glamor. even mage conceits that vampire blood is effectively Tass. so while for the most part each setting gives its own flavor and should be referred to each respective name by each respective game line, fundamentally there is little difference between the different critters and the magical energy they use to perform their powers. <br /> <br /> now I'm not terribly familiar with demon but I'd say True Faith is probably the most powerful force in the game setting and across several game lines, it can do just about anything with out carrying Resonance and incurring paradox doesn't have a finite number of points and is effectively its own power source. it also happens to be the rarest of all the powers I've seen in any World of Darkness setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T02:43:19-07:00","id":142205,"title":"","content":"It comes down to &quot;Bang for the buck&quot; vs. &quot;Ease of gathering it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, Glamour's going to sit this competition out. It's tricky to get, and it just doesn't do much. You have to spend days, maybe weeks patronizing an artist (or an hour mindraping someone) just to squeeze out a dribble of something that is only used to make your cantrips easier to cast... which you only want anyway because the Changeling magic difficulties are kinda off the deep end. Also if you play with it too much you go completely bonkers.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is sitting there comforting Glamour; like Glamour it's only good for casting magic spells (though hey, at least it's decent magic) and... unless you have merits, it's pretty tough to regain outside a very limited region of the world.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is stumbling along at the tail end of the pack. Yes, yes, it can feul sphere magic... but you don't <i>need it</i> in order to do that. Unfortunately that's pretty much all that it does, it makes a great thing a little bit better. It's the cherry on top. It's <i>relatively</i> easy to get... but the volume you can have at any time is limited, without investing in Prime or tass.<br /> <br /> Then you have Pathos. it fuels magic powers <i>and</i> can heal your corpus. Otherwise it's about as exciting as the name &quot;pathos&quot; would indicate.<br /> <br /> Just ahead is Gnosis. The <i>points</i> aren't useful for much besides powering Gifts... but the <i>rating</i> is <i>also</i> used for Gifts, it's used for crossing the Gauntlet, peeking through the Gauntlet, activating fetishes, and sometimes can even grant you premonitions and visions. It's no harder to regain than Quintessence, and increasing your Gnosis through experience is vastly easier than increasing your Avatar rating that way...<br /> <br /> Ahead of those two, Blood and Chi are nearly neck-and-neck, with Blood having the edge. Sure, Chi can power generally better Disciplines, and can be used to give your character natural claws and fangs and whatnot... but... can it create ghouls? Can it boost your attributes? Is it in a literally unlimited supply available to you? Plus Kindred don't go wacky worrying about the &quot;flavor&quot; of their blood, like Kuei-Jin do with the aspect of their Chi. Since they come from the same sources (for the general PC, anyway) and can actually be kind of tricky to get (seriously, I dunno why blood-sucking predators are supposedly able to feed easily. But I digress) and they're roughly equal.<br /> <br /> Then you have Rage. oh boy, Rage. Rage is frankly an amazing trait. It gives you extras actions on a one-for-one basis. You don't have to have Wayfare, or Time, or Celerity to get that, you're born with it. Not just that, but you can use it to shake off stuns. You can use it to ignore wound penalties. In Wild west you could use it to Auto-intimidate someone. You can use it to instantly assume any form you want. That's just the spendable points; Rage is literally the ONLY trait that you roll in order to tell the dice, &quot;screw you i don't <i>feel like</i> dying! And of course, both points and rating fuel a nigh infinite number of Gifts. And on top of that, it's really easy to regain. Is the moon there? Gain Rage. Is a fight starting? Did you take a hit? Gain rage. Did your packmate take a hit? Gain rage. Did you botch? Gain rage. are you being insulted? gain rage. Do you have Silver Claws? Gain rage forever. It has exactly two drawbacks, both of them negligible; You frenzy, but you can spend Willpower to <i>not</i> Frenzy.. .and when you're in a frenzy you're immune to wound penalties, which is actually pretty nice in a lot of the instances where frenzy is going to come up in a lot of games (your ST needs to be a sadist to make you roll Frenzy if you head off with a kinfolk at the moot's revel, after all) aaaaand it can give you a social penalty among humans, and if it's higher than your Willpower, even among other Garou. Thing is, if you have high Rage on your character, you probably never intended to be the people person <i>anyway</i>. And you actually have to try to build a character with the latter problem; they're each one-point traits on the Freebie chart, was that extra dot of Technology so important?<br /> <br /> Yes, unless you're a Gurahl, Rage is near the finish line...<br /> <br /> And then you have Faith from Demon, which you can use to do get your crazy-form, power your powers, create thralls, and a bunch of other stuff beyond my ken because I've only thumbed the book... Since I'm not really knowledgeable about Demon, I'm not sure where Faith falls, but it seems, on the surface, to be a little bit ahead of Rage - maybe not quite that versatile, but it's not terribly hard to gain, and, well, Rage is more likely to destroy a gang of empowered mooks than it is to create them. Seriously,as with Blood, the ability to make pseudo-supernatural buddies with the power is pretty nice.<br /> <br /> conviction is the dark Horse. it's not <i>powerful</i> (though it can certainly be a pain in the ass if you're on the wrong end of it) but in terms of economy, it is fabulous. You spend a point... and you get a laundry list of abilities, all just for that one point. Regaining it is a little convoluted, but not <i>terribly</i> difficult (most of the difficulty of regaining conviction seems based on the fact that if you're an Imbued cracking out edges, you stand a good chance of not living long enough to get hte Conviction back, rather than the system itself). So... yeah. You can't build an army of hte night with it, and you can't use it to demand a backsie from death... but a little bit of it goes a SUPER long way with what it <i>does</i> let you do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T17:57:13-07:00","id":149043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/138976-what-source-of-energy-power-is-the-strongest?p=142205#post142205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you have Pathos. it fuels magic powers <i>and</i> can heal your corpus. Otherwise it's about as exciting as the name &quot;pathos&quot; would indicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cat Came Back's assessment is pretty spot-on. The one thing I would add, if we're looking at all the groups, is Vitality. In Orpheus, once Pathos undergoes the metaphysical changes of a post-Wraith universe, Vitality blows most of the other power pools out of the water. It's super-easy to recover, even regenerating on its own at a fairly rapid rate (up to one-per-hour for Skimmers) and you can burn Willpower to get a boost of 3 Vitality when you need it (to the point where that pretty much becomes Willpower's primary function in Orpheus). Not only is it easy to get and regain, but the bang-for-buck on how Vitality fuels Horrors (and how quickly the scaling for Horrors can do some mind-blowing stuff for a tiny bit of Vitality at higher Tiers) coupled with group synergy when used to fuel Benefits (for only a measly 1 Vitality) goes beyond potent. Not to mention Vitality Emblems. So, yeah, in my estimation, I'd place Vitality very high on the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3098-theblockknight","name":"TheBlockKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T05:44:21-07:00","id":149335,"title":"","content":"Q: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/138976-what-source-of-energy-power-is-the-strongest#post138976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What source of energy/power is the strongest?</div> </div> </div> </div>A: Willpower.<br /> <br /> it can easily regained by sleeping, by meditation or supernatural powers. its universally usefull for anyone, to do anything.<br /> It can provide auto-successes, its used for feats of strength, is needet to fuel some powers, to roll some powers(Thau), and you can ignore penalties from pain (so its worth 5 dice when crippled, and even more Dice when ignoring supernatural pain like from Touch of agony from Valeren).<br /> <br /> Be a vampire, take the psychic-vampre Flaw so you only regain WP for drinking 3 pts of blood. take Efficient Digestion Merit -&gt; gain 1 WP per 2 Bloodpoints (converted to 3) taken, add daredevil merit and lets rock!<br /> <br /> Willpower is the most powerfull Powersource in the world of darkness, And its one freaking 1 Freeb per point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T14:17:29-07:00","id":149722,"title":"","content":"Eadee, don't forget the old Self-Confident Merit. Dumbest Merit in the game... well, that and Indomitable Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:08:22-07:00","id":149772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/138976-what-source-of-energy-power-is-the-strongest?p=149722#post149722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eadee, don't forget the old Self-Confident Merit. Dumbest Merit in the game... well, that and Indomitable Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I kinda forgot that one ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:02:53-07:00","id":150408,"title":"","content":"I'm reading the OP asking about the strongest force when applied through some PC based Medium, as he references his friend coming up with a technique that let him use Gnosis to do agg to his surroundings.<br /> <br /> Looking at pure power sources, without the bells and whistles to enact them, Rage and Blood Pool are probably the strongest right out of the gate. Both can beef up combat with effectively no training or abilities needed.<br /> <br /> With bells and whistles, such as Spheres, Gifts, Charms and Disciplines (ok fine, and Arcanoi and Powers and whatever Demons and Mummies and ok, not fine, nevermind..) scaling the powers comes out quite a bit more difficult.<br /> <br /> Blood and Rage, for example are finite resources, where Glamour, Quintessence and (I believe) Gnosis can all be collected and pooled into &quot;Magical Items&quot; common to the species. I suppose Blood can do this, in the form of very specific Thaum rituals, but not with the ease and frequency the other species have.<br /> <br /> It's basically impossible to rate any of the supernatural power sources without a complex breakdown of the most powerful individual powers that said power sources are used for. While I do think this would be an interesting intellectual pursuit, I also think that trying to do it on a webforum will ultimately devolve into line-based-fandom slap fights.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*On Behalf of Mage I have to point out that Quintessence = raw aggravated damage, or a shitload of extra agg dice when pumped into anything with a basic Prime 2 effect. This also ignores the terrifying scope of Primal Utility..</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2599-professor-absinthe","name":"Professor Absinthe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2599_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}